{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For a curse of Elohim is hanged.</b> It is an affront to the King — for man is made in the likeness of His image, and Israel are His sons. A parable: two twin brothers who resembled one another; one became king and one was seized for banditry and hanged. Everyone who saw him said, 'The king is hanged.' Every 'curse' in Scripture is a term of belittlement and contempt, as in ״וְהוּא קִלְלַנִי קְלָלָה נִמְרֶצֶת״ (1 Kings 2)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:55.336879436Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}